          "conclusion_handle": "c_share",
          "strongest_objection": "The explicit confidentiality policy contains no emergency exception; obeying it is a standing duty that should not be unilaterally overridden.",
          "answer_to_objection": "The priority premise holds that saving the patient from serious, otherwise unavoidable harm is a stronger moral duty than rigid policy adherence, provided disclosure is strictly minimal.",
          "reversal_condition": "If the same medical safety could be achieved without any disclosure (e.g., via known standard protocols or delayed until consent), then the policy duty would again take precedence and Mara should withhold the information."
